{"markdown": "Jina Embeddings\n==========\n\nQdrant is compatible with [Jina AI](https://jina.ai/) embeddings. You can get a free trial key from [Jina Embeddings](https://jina.ai/embeddings/) to get embeddings.\n\nQdrant users can receive a 10% discount on Jina AI APIs by using the code **QDRANT**.\n\nTechnical Summary\n----------\n\n|          Model           |                 Dimension                  |            Language            |MRL (matryoshka)|       Context        |\n|--------------------------|--------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|----------------|----------------------|\n|  **jina-embeddings-v4**  |**2048 (single-vector), 128 (multi-vector)**|     **Multilingual (30+)**     |    **Yes**     |**32768 + Text/Image**|\n|       jina-clip-v2       |                    1024                    |Multilingual (100+, focus on 30)|      Yes       |      Text/Image      |\n|    jina-embeddings-v3    |                    1024                    |  Multilingual (89 languages)   |      Yes       |         8192         |\n|jina-embeddings-v2-base-en|                    768                     |            English             |       No       |         8192         |\n|jina-embeddings-v2-base-de|                    768                     |        German & English        |       No       |         8192         |\n|jina-embeddings-v2-base-es|                    768                     |       Spanish & English        |       No       |         8192         |\n|jina-embeddings-v2-base-zh|                    768                     |       Chinese & English        |       No       |         8192         |\n\n>\n>\n> Jina recommends using `jina-embeddings-v4` for all tasks.\n>\n>\n\nOn top of the backbone, `jina-embeddings-v4` has been trained with 5 task-specific adapters for different embedding uses. Include `task` in your request to optimize your downstream application:\n\n* **retrieval.query**: Used to encode user queries or questions in retrieval tasks.\n* **retrieval.passage**: Used to encode large documents in retrieval tasks at indexing time.\n* **code.query**: Used to encode user queries or questions in code related retrieval tasks.\n* **code.passage**: Used to encode large documents in code related retrieval tasks at indexing time.\n* **text-matching**: Used to encode text for similarity matching, such as measuring similarity between two sentences.\n\nSimilarly, `jina-embeddings-v3` has been trained with 5 task-specific adapters for different embedding uses. Include `task` in your request to optimize your downstream application:\n\n* **retrieval.query**: Used to encode user queries or questions in retrieval tasks.\n* **retrieval.passage**: Used to encode large documents in retrieval tasks at indexing time.\n* **classification**: Used to encode text for text classification tasks.\n* **text-matching**: Used to encode text for similarity matching, such as measuring similarity between two sentences.\n* **separation**: Used for clustering or reranking tasks.\n\n`jina-embeddings-v4`, `jina-embeddings-v3` and `jina-clip-v2` support **Matryoshka Representation Learning**, allowing users to control the embedding dimension with minimal performance loss.\nInclude `dimensions` in your request to select the desired dimension.\nBy default, **dimensions** is set to 2048 (`jina-embeddings-v4`) or 1024 (`jina-embeddings-v3` and `jina-clip-v2`), and a number between 256 and 2048 is recommended.\nYou can reference the table below for hints on dimension vs. performance for the `jina-embeddings-v3` model. Similar results hold for the others.\n\n|               Dimension               | 32  | 64  | 128 | 256 | 512 |768 |1024 |\n|---------------------------------------|-----|-----|-----|-----|-----|----|-----|\n|Average Retrieval Performance (nDCG@10)|52.54|58.54|61.64|62.72|63.16|63.3|63.35|\n\n`jina-embeddings-v4` and `jina-embeddings-v3` supports [Late Chunking](https://jina.ai/news/late-chunking-in-long-context-embedding-models/), the technique to leverage the model’s long-context capabilities for generating contextual chunk embeddings. Include `late_chunking=True` in your request to enable contextual chunked representation. When set to true, Jina AI API will concatenate all sentences in the input field and feed them as a single string to the model. Internally, the model embeds this long concatenated string and then performs late chunking, returning a list of embeddings that matches the size of the input list.\n\nExample\n----------\n\n### Text-to-Text Retrieval ###\n\nThe code below demonstrates how to use `jina-embeddings-v4` with Qdrant:\n\n```\nimport requests\n\nimport qdrant_client\nfrom qdrant_client.models import Distance, VectorParams, Batch\n\n# Provide Jina API key and choose one of the available models.\nJINA_API_KEY = \"jina_xxxxxxxxxxx\"\nMODEL = \"jina-embeddings-v4\"\nDIMENSIONS = 2048 # Or choose your desired output vector dimensionality.\nTASK = 'retrieval.passage' # For indexing, or set to retrieval.query for querying\n\n# Get embeddings from the API\nurl = \"https://api.jina.ai/v1/embeddings\"\n\nheaders = {\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {JINA_API_KEY}\",\n}\n\ndata = {\n    \"input\": [\"Your text string goes here\", \"You can send multiple texts\"],\n    \"model\": MODEL,\n    \"dimensions\": DIMENSIONS,\n    \"task\": TASK,\n    \"late_chunking\": True,\n}\n\nresponse = requests.post(url, headers=headers, json=data)\nembeddings = [d[\"embedding\"] for d in response.json()[\"data\"]]\n\n# Index the embeddings into Qdrant\nclient = qdrant_client.QdrantClient(\":memory:\")\nclient.create_collection(\n    collection_name=\"MyCollection\",\n    vectors_config=VectorParams(size= DIMENSIONS, distance=Distance.DOT),\n)\n\nqdrant_client.upsert(\n    collection_name=\"MyCollection\",\n    points=Batch(\n        ids=list(range(len(embeddings))),\n        vectors=embeddings,\n    ),\n)\n\n```\n\n### Text-to-Image Retrieval ###\n\nThe code below demonstrates how to use `jina-embeddings-v4` with Qdrant:\n\n```\nimport requests\nfrom qdrant_client import QdrantClient\nfrom qdrant_client.models import Distance, VectorParams, PointStruct\n\n# Provide your Jina API key and choose the model.\nJINA_API_KEY = \"jina_xxxxxxxxxxx\"\nMODEL = \"jina-embeddings-v4\"\nDIMENSIONS = 2048  # Set the desired output vector dimensionality.\n\n# Define the inputs\ntext_input = \"A blue cat\"\nimage_url = \"https://i.pinimg.com/600x315/21/48/7e/21487e8e0970dd366dafaed6ab25d8d8.jpg\"\n\n# Get embeddings from the Jina API\nurl = \"https://api.jina.ai/v1/embeddings\"\nheaders = {\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {JINA_API_KEY}\",\n}\ndata = {\n    \"input\": [\n        {\"text\": text_input},\n        {\"image\": image_url},\n    ],\n    \"model\": MODEL,\n    \"dimensions\": DIMENSIONS,\n}\n\nresponse = requests.post(url, headers=headers, json=data)\nresponse_data = response.json()[\"data\"]\n\n# The model doesn't differentiate between images and text, so we extract output based on the input order.\ntext_embedding = response_data[0][\"embedding\"]\nimage_embedding = response_data[1][\"embedding\"]\n\n# Initialize Qdrant client\nclient = QdrantClient(url=\"http://localhost:6333/\")\n\n# Create a collection with named vectors\ncollection_name = \"MyCollection\"\nclient.recreate_collection(\n    collection_name=collection_name,\n    vectors_config={\n        \"text_vector\": VectorParams(size=DIMENSIONS, distance=Distance.DOT),\n        \"image_vector\": VectorParams(size=DIMENSIONS, distance=Distance.DOT),\n    },\n)\n\nclient.upsert(\n    collection_name=collection_name,\n    points=[\n        PointStruct(\n            id=0,\n            vector={\n                \"text_vector\": text_embedding,\n                \"image_vector\": image_embedding,\n            }\n        )\n    ],\n)\n\n# Now let's query the collection\nsearch_query = \"A purple cat\"\n\n# Get the embedding for the search query from the Jina API\nurl = \"https://api.jina.ai/v1/embeddings\"\nheaders = {\n    \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n    \"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {JINA_API_KEY}\",\n}\ndata = {\n    \"input\": [{\"text\": search_query}],\n    \"model\": MODEL,\n    \"dimensions\": DIMENSIONS,\n    # \"task\": \"retrieval.query\" # Uncomment this line for text-to-text retrieval tasks\n}\n\nresponse = requests.post(url, headers=headers, json=data)\nquery_embedding = response.json()[\"data\"][0][\"embedding\"]\n\nsearch_results = client.query_points(\n    collection_name=collection_name,\n    query=query_embedding,\n    using=\"image_vector\",\n    limit=5\n).points\n\nfor result in search_results:\n    print(f\"ID: {result.id}, Score: {result.score}\")\n\n```", "links": [["https://qdrant.tech/", ""], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/", "Develop"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/deploy-intro/", "Deploy"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/ecosystem/", "Ecosystem"], ["https://qdrant.tech/learn/", "Learn"], ["https://api.qdrant.tech/api-reference", "API Reference"], ["https://cloud.qdrant.io/login", "Log in"], ["https://cloud.qdrant.io/signup", "Start Free"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/", "Migration Tool"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-pinecone/", "From Pinecone"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-weaviate/", "From Weaviate"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-milvus/", "From Milvus"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-elasticsearch/", "From Elasticsearch"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-opensearch/", "From OpenSearch"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-azure-search/", "From Azure AI Search"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-pgvector/", "From pgvector"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-s3-vectors/", "From S3 Vectors"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-chroma/", "From Chroma"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-redis/", "From Redis"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-mongodb/", "From MongoDB"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-faiss/", "From FAISS"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-solr/", "From Apache Solr"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migrate-to-qdrant/from-qdrant/", "From Qdrant"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/", "Migration Guidance"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/pre-migration-baseline/", "Pre-Migration Baseline"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/data-integrity/", "Data Integrity"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/search-quality/", "Search Quality"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/migration-guidance/diagnosing-discrepancies/", "Diagnosing Discrepancies"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-synchronization/", "Data Synchronization"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-synchronization/with-postgres/", "Keeping Postgres and Qdrant in Sync"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/", "Data Management"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/airbyte/", "Airbyte"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/airflow/", "Apache Airflow"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/spark/", "Apache Spark"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/chonkie/", "Chonkie"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/cocoindex/", "CocoIndex"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/confluent/", "Confluent Kafka"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/dlt/", "DLT"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/fluvio/", "InfinyOn Fluvio"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/poma/", "POMA"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/redpanda/", "Redpanda Connect"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/data-management/unstructured/", "Unstructured"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/", "Embeddings"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/aleph-alpha/", "Aleph Alpha"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/bedrock/", "AWS Bedrock"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/cohere/", "Cohere"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/fusion-embedding-2/", "Fusion Embedding 2"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/gemini/", "Gemini"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/jina-embeddings/", "Jina Embeddings"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/mistral/", "Mistral"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/mixedbread/", "MixedBread"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/mixpeek/", "Mixpeek"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/nomic/", "Nomic"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/nvidia/", "Nvidia"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/ollama/", "Ollama"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/openai/", "OpenAI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/premai/", "Prem AI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/snowflake/", "Snowflake Models"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/superlinked/", "Superlinked"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/twelvelabs/", "Twelve Labs"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/upstage/", "Upstage"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/voyage/", "Voyage AI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/", "Frameworks"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/agno/", "Agno"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/autogen/", "AutoGen"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/lakechain/", "AWS Lakechain"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/camel/", "CamelAI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/cheshire-cat/", "Cheshire Cat"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/cognee/", "Cognee"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/crewai/", "CrewAI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/dagster/", "Dagster"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/deepeval/", "DeepEval"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/dynamiq/", "Dynamiq"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/feast/", "Feast"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/fifty-one/", "FiftyOne"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/genkit/", "Firebase Genkit"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/google-adk/", "Google ADK"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/haystack/", "Haystack"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/honeyhive/", "HoneyHive"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/langchain/", "LangChain"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/langchain4j/", "LangChain4j"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/langgraph/", "LangGraph"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/llama-index/", "LlamaIndex"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/mastra/", "Mastra"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/mem0/", "Mem0"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/microsoft-graphrag/", "Microsoft GraphRAG"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/nlweb/", "Microsoft NLWeb"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/neo4j-graphrag/", "Neo4j GraphRAG"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/rig-rs/", "Rig-rs"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/rocketride/", "RocketRide"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/semantic-router/", "Semantic-Router"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/smolagents/", "SmolAgents"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/spring-ai/", "Spring AI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/dspy/", "Stanford DSPy"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/swiftide/", "Swiftide"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/sycamore/", "Sycamore"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/testcontainers/", "Testcontainers"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/txtai/", "txtai"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/vanna-ai/", "Vanna.AI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/mirror-security/", "VectaX - Mirror Security"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/frameworks/voltagent/", "VoltAgent"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/observability/", "Observability"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/observability/openllmetry/", "OpenLLMetry"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/observability/openlit/", "OpenLIT"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/observability/datadog/", "Datadog"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/", "Platforms"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/apify/", "Apify"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/buildship/", "BuildShip"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/keboola/", "Keboola"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/kotaemon/", "Kotaemon"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/make/", "Make.com"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/n8n/", "N8N"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/pipedream/", "Pipedream"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/powerapps/", "Power Apps"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/privategpt/", "PrivateGPT"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/mulesoft/", "Salesforce Mulesoft"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/tooljet/", "ToolJet"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/platforms/vectorize/", "Vectorize.io"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/", "Essential Examples"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/agentic-rag-crewai-zoom/", "Agentic RAG with CrewAI"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/agentic-rag-camelai-discord/", "Discord RAG Bot"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/rag-deepseek/", "5-Minute RAG with DeepSeek"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/qdrant-n8n/", "n8n Workflow Automation"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/video-anomaly-edge-part-1/", "Video Anomaly Detection Part 1: Architecture, Twelve Labs, and NVIDIA VSS"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/video-anomaly-edge-part-2/", "Video Anomaly Detection Part 2: Edge-to-Cloud Pipeline"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/tutorials-build-essentials/video-anomaly-edge-part-3/", "Video Anomaly Detection Part 3: Scoring, Governance, and Deployment"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/", "Build Prototypes"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/graphrag-qdrant-neo4j/", "GraphRAG with Qdrant and Neo4j"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/qdrant-dspy-medicalbot/", "Building a Chain-of-Thought Medical Chatbot with Qdrant and DSPy"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/llama-index-multitenancy/", "Multitenancy with LlamaIndex"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-chatbot-red-hat-openshift-haystack/", "Private Chatbot for Interactive Learning"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/cohere-rag-connector/", "Implement Cohere RAG connector"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-customer-support-cohere-airbyte-aws/", "Question-Answering System for AI Customer Support"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/hybrid-search-llamaindex-jinaai/", "Chat With Product PDF Manuals Using Hybrid Search"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-contract-management-stackit-aleph-alpha/", "Region-Specific Contract Management System"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/natural-language-search-oracle-cloud-infrastructure-cohere-langchain/", "RAG System for Employee Onboarding"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-chatbot-vultr-dspy-ollama/", "Private RAG Information Extraction Engine"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/recommendation-system-ovhcloud/", "Movie Recommendation System"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/examples/rag-chatbot-scaleway/", "Blog-Reading Chatbot with GPT-4o"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/improve-search/", "Improve Search"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/improve-search/retrieval-relevance/", "Measuring Retrieval Relevance"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/improve-search/pipeline-output-quality/", "Evaluating Pipeline Output Quality"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/improve-search/query-decomposition/", "Query Decomposition for Multi-Hop Questions"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/datasets/", "Practice Datasets"], ["https://jina.ai/", "Jina AI"], ["https://jina.ai/embeddings/", "Jina Embeddings"], ["https://jina.ai/news/late-chunking-in-long-context-embedding-models/", "Late Chunking"], ["https://qdrant.tech/github.com/qdrant/landing_page/tree/master/qdrant-landing/content/documentation/embeddings/jina-embeddings.md", "edit"], ["https://github.com/qdrant/landing_page/issues/new/choose", "create"], ["https://qdrant.tech/documentation/embeddings/jina-embeddings/index.md", "View as Markdown"], ["https://github.com/qdrant/landing_page/tree/master/qdrant-landing/content/documentation/embeddings/jina-embeddings.md", "Edit on Github"], ["https://qdrant.to/cloud/", "Start Free"], ["https://qdrant.tech/legal/terms_and_conditions/", "Terms"], ["https://qdrant.tech/legal/privacy-policy/", "Privacy Policy"], ["https://qdrant.tech/legal/impressum/", "Impressum"], ["https://qdrant.tech/legal/recruitment-privacy-policy/", "Recruitment Privacy Policy"]], "meta": {"meta": {"title": "Jina Embeddings - Qdrant", "description": "Use Jina AI embeddings with Qdrant for multilingual semantic search, code retrieval, and long-context indexing with task-specific adapters and Matryoshka dimensions.", "keyw